{
 "_note": "MMD common morph catalog: what a morph NAME means, and how models usually implement it. This file is a knowledge base, not a mapping table - it says nothing about DIVA. A name's entry here is evidence about semantics only; the geometry a morph actually produces is always measured from the source PMX (see morph_effect.py). Entries are ordered so more specific names are tested before more general ones.",
 "_sources": [
  "PMX 2.0/2.1 spec panel bytes: 0 system, 1 eyebrow, 2 eye, 3 mouth, 4 other (PMX 仕様書 by 極北P)",
  "community morph usage over 483 distributed motions (lilxyzw's mmd_morph_names_all.txt): あ 90.9%, まばたき 87.6%, お 87.6%, い 86.7%, う 81.2%, 笑い 68.7%, 困る 49.1%, え 46.4%, 下 40.4%, 怒り 28.4%, ウィンク 27.1%, 上 25.7%, 真面目 23.2%, にやり 22.8%, 瞳小 19.9%, にこり 17.6%, はぅ 17.2%, ウィンク右 11.8%, じと目 10.4%, びっくり 9.9%, なごみ 7.7%, ワ 7.5%, にっこり 5.0%",
  "measured on this machine: 10 real PMX models (see rev/pmx_*.json and the morph census) and 13 real VMDs"
 ],
 "_usage_pct_note": "usage_pct is the share of 483 distributed motions that animate the name; it is a priority hint, never a mapping.",
 "_panel_note": "panel is the expected PMX panel byte. A disagreement between the name's expected panel and the file's panel is evidence about the model, not proof the name is wrong.",

